.TH RUSTQUERY 1 "2026-10-24" "RustQuery" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustquery \- desktop SQL workbench for PostgreSQL, MySQL and SQLite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustquery
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B RustQuery
is a native desktop SQL client for PostgreSQL, MySQL and SQLite. It keeps
saved connection profiles, browses schemas lazily, runs multi-statement SQL
from several editor tabs, and displays results in a virtualised, sortable and
filterable grid. Results can be exported as CSV, JSON or SQL INSERT statements.
.PP
The application runs in a single window with a menu bar, connection dashboard,
schema explorer, SQL editor, result grid and timestamped console. SQL file
dialogs use the desktop's native file chooser where available; exports use an
in-application dialog.
.PP
PostgreSQL and MySQL sessions connect over the network. SQLite databases are
opened locally as a file, or in memory with the special path
\fB:memory:\fR.
No configuration is required to start the program: create a profile on the
connection dashboard, select it, and choose \fBConnect\fR.
.PP
A graphical session with OpenGL support is required. RustQuery uses X11 or
Wayland on Linux.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Read and write profiles, settings, history and workspace state in
.IR PATH .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short help text and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUSTQUERY_CONFIG_DIR
Overrides the configuration directory. Takes precedence over
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME .
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
When set, configuration is stored in
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/rustquery .
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate
.I ~/.config/rustquery
when the variables above are not set.
.TP
.B DISPLAY
The X11 display used when running under X11.
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The Wayland compositor socket used when running under Wayland.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustquery/profiles.json
Saved connection profiles. Passwords are stored in plain text; the file is
created with mode 0600 on Unix.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustquery/settings.json
Theme, row limit, query timeout and layout preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustquery/history.json
Query history.
.TP
.I ~/.config/rustquery/workspace.json
Restored editor tabs.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B F1
Open the complete in-application keyboard reference.
.TP
.B F2
Show the connection dashboard or return to the workspace.
.TP
.BR F3 ", " F4 ", " F6 ", " F7
Focus the explorer, editor, results grid or console.
.TP
.BR F5 " or " Ctrl+Enter
Execute the selection, or the whole editor buffer when nothing is selected.
.TP
.BR F8 ", " F9 ", " F10
Begin, commit or roll back a transaction.
.TP
.BR F11 " or " Ctrl+,
Open settings.
.TP
.B F12
Cycle the colour theme.
.TP
.B Ctrl+H
Open query history.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D
Disconnect from the database.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit. A confirmation is shown while a query is running or a transaction is
open.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+T " / " Ctrl+W
Open or close a query tab.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+Tab " / " Ctrl+Shift+Tab
Switch to the next or previous query tab.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Space
Open schema and keyword completion in the editor.
.TP
.BR Ctrl+O " / " Ctrl+S
Open or save a SQL file.
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
Export the current result set.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Filter all columns in the result grid.
.SH EXAMPLES
Start with the default configuration:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
rustquery
.EE
.RE
.PP
Use an isolated configuration directory for testing:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
rustquery \-\-config\-dir /tmp/rustquery-config
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on a normal exit. A non-zero status is returned when the desktop window
cannot be initialised, the async runtime cannot start, or command-line
arguments are invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR psql (1),
.BR mysql (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
